            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "`config.autowrite = true` (which is default) means that [**current** session will be written before closing Neovim](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/aac602e097b99a06bc84e43356f080eb6256dd21/doc/mini-sessions.txt#L80). In your example there is no loaded/read session. Try these steps:\r\n- Execute `:lua MiniSessions.write('my_session')` after opening Neovim, which will also make 'my_session' the current one.\r\n- Make some changes, like open a few buffers.\r\n- Close Neovim.\r\n- Open Neovim. The session 'my_session' should be listed.\r\n- Load 'my_session' session. It should show changes you made before closing Neovim.\r\n\r\nClosing as it is working as intended.",
