            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> @echasnovski is it possible to automatically create a session before closing Neovim if it doesn't exist in the first place?\r\n\r\nNot sure I understand the question. Do you want to create a session if Neovim currently is not in a session? It is possible by creating an autocommand on `VimLeavePre` and disabling `autowrite`. Like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.sessions').setup({ autowrite = false })\r\n\r\nlocal autowrite = function()\r\n  local session_name\r\n  -- ~rite session with default name even if not currently in session\r\n  if vim.v.this_session == '' then session_name = 'default' end\r\n  MiniSessions.write(session_name, { force = true })\r\nend\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('VimLeavePre', { callback = autowrite, desc = 'Autowrite session' })\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2023-09-11T17:45:59Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/427#issuecomment-1714325170",
            "id": 1714325170,
